"""Hand-written English method descriptions, part 4: equipment Kettlebell.

Keyed by the v5 catalog slug (slugify of the canonical exercise name).
Merged by build_progression.py as the last description tier; a key that
matches no catalog row fails the build, so typos surface immediately.
"""

DESCRIPTIONS = {
    "chest_supported_kettlebell_row": "The chest-supported kettlebell row rows two bells from an incline bench with the chest pinned, taking all momentum out of the pull. Squeeze the shoulder blades together at the top and let the arms hang fully at the bottom; the back, not the arms, should ache after.",
    "double_kettlebell_bicep_curl": "The double kettlebell bicep curl curls two bells together or alternately, front-loading the frame and doubling the grip demand. Keep the elbows pinned and the wrists neutral; the racked start position is half the core workout.",
    "double_kettlebell_clean": "The double kettlebell clean drives two bells from the swing into the rack in one hip-powered motion. It is the gateway to double presses and front squats; punch the hands through rather than muscling the bells around the wrists.",
    "double_kettlebell_clean_and_press": "The double kettlebell clean and press chains a clean of both bells into a strict overhead press of both, then returns them under control. It is a brutal full-body strength and conditioning lift; every rep should start and end with crisp rack positions.",
    "double_kettlebell_dead_clean": "The double kettlebell dead clean starts with both bells dead on the floor and cleans them to the rack in one pull. Starting from a dead stop removes the swing, so the pull is pure hip power; reset the setup each rep for the strictest version.",
    "double_kettlebell_dead_split_snatch": "The double kettlebell dead split snatch pulls two dead bells from the floor and drives them overhead with a split stance catch. It is an advanced, explosive full-body lift; master the double clean and the split jerk separately before blending them.",
    "double_kettlebell_jerk": "The double kettlebell jerk drives two racked bells overhead with a short dip and a punch of the legs, catching with straight arms. It moves far more load than the strict press and taxes the whole body; keep the dip shallow and the catch fast.",
    "double_kettlebell_overhead_carry": "The double kettlebell overhead carry walks with a bell locked out in each hand, doubling the stability demand of the single version. The core must hold the ribcage down while the shoulders hold the lockout; short, frequent sets beat sloppy long ones.",
    "double_kettlebell_overhead_press": "The double kettlebell overhead press presses two racked bells strictly overhead, loading the shoulders, triceps and trunk symmetrically. Keep the wrists stacked and the ribs down; the legs are quiet, as this is a press, not a push.",
    "double_kettlebell_rear_delt_row": "The double kettlebell rear delt row hinges forward and rows two bells high toward the chest with the elbows flared. The wide pull biases the rear delts and upper back; keep the torso close to parallel and the neck long.",
    "double_kettlebell_row": "The double kettlebell row hinges and rows two bells to the ribs together, loading the lats and grip symmetrically. Keep the back flat and let the hips and core hold the hinge; the bells' pull makes balance part of the exercise.",
    "double_kettlebell_split_jerk": "The double kettlebell split jerk drives two racked bells overhead with a dip and a split-leg catch, the most load the overhead press family can move. Drop under the bells rather than pressing them up; recover the feet in order: front, back, together.",
    "double_kettlebell_swing_snatch": "The double kettlebell swing snatch sends two swinging bells overhead in one violent, hip-driven motion. It is among the most demanding kettlebell lifts; own the double swing and double clean first, and expect the grip to give out before the hips do.",
    "floor_kettlebell_pullover": "The floor kettlebell pullover arcs a bell from the chest to beyond the head and back while lying on the floor, stretching the lats under a light load. The floor keeps the ribs honest; stop the arc if the lower back leaves the ground.",
    "kettlebell_bulgarian_split_squat": "The kettlebell Bulgarian split squat loads a rear-foot-elevated split squat with one or two bells held at the chest or at the sides. The kettlebell's pull keeps the torso honest; sink the back knee and drive up through the front heel.",
    "kettlebell_close_grip_floor_press": "The kettlebell close-grip floor press lies on the floor and presses two bells with the elbows tucked close to the ribs. The floor stops the elbow safely and the narrow path loads the triceps hard; pause when the upper arms settle before the next rep.",
    "kettlebell_concentration_curl": "The kettlebell concentration curl braces the working elbow against the inner thigh and curls a bell in strict isolation. The brace removes every shortcut; squeeze at the top and lower slowly under control.",
    "kettlebell_farmer_s_walk": "The kettlebell farmer's walk carries a heavy bell in each hand for distance or time. The grip, traps and core hold everything together while the legs walk; stay tall, keep the shoulders packed and take short, quick steps.",
    "kettlebell_goblet_lunge": "The kettlebell goblet lunge holds a bell at the chest through lunges, front-loading the torso so the core works as hard as the legs. The counterweight makes it easy to keep the spine tall; step or walk, and keep the front knee tracking over the shoe.",
    "kettlebell_halo": "The kettlebell halo circles a bell around the head at collarbone height, training shoulder mobility and core control. Keep the hips quiet, since the movement belongs to the shoulders and ribs; reverse directions halfway through each set.",
    "kettlebell_hammer_curl": "The kettlebell hammer curl curls the bell by its handle with the wrist neutral, biasing the brachialis and forearm. Keep the elbow pinned to the side and let the bell rotate naturally in the hand.",
    "kettlebell_hip_thrust": "The kettlebell hip thrust drives the hips to full extension with a bell padded across the pelvis. The single-bell setup needs no bar or bench changes; squeeze the glutes hard at the top and keep the chin tucked.",
    "kettlebell_kickstand_deadlift": "The kettlebell kickstand deadlift hinges with one foot's toe kicked back behind the other, splitting the difference between a bilateral and a single-leg pattern. The rear leg is a kickstand, not a worker; keep the weight over the front leg and push the hips back.",
    "kettlebell_lunge_press": "The kettlebell lunge press steps into a lunge and presses the bell overhead as the knee descends. The legs create instability that the pressing shoulder must absorb; alternate legs and keep the wrist stacked over the elbow.",
    "kettlebell_offset_reverse_lunge_and_press": "The kettlebell offset reverse lunge and press holds the bell on one side while stepping back and pressing it up, forcing the core to fight the off-center load through the whole rep. Keep the torso square to the front; the offset is the point.",
    "kettlebell_overhead_carry": "The kettlebell overhead carry walks with a bell locked out overhead, training shoulder stability, core strength and grip in one drill. Keep the bicep near the ear and the ribcage stacked over the pelvis; switch hands at the halfway mark.",
    "kettlebell_overhead_tricep_extension": "The kettlebell overhead tricep extension lowers a bell behind the head from a locked-out overhead grip and presses it back up. Keep the elbows pointing forward and the ribs down; the stretch at the bottom is the growth position.",
    "kettlebell_pistol_squat": "The kettlebell pistol squat holds a bell at the chest as counterweight while squatting on one leg. The weight shifts the balance point backward, making the hardest part of the pistol, staying over the foot, far more manageable.",
    "kettlebell_pullover": "The kettlebell pullover arcs a bell from the chest to behind the head and back while lying down, stretching the lats and demanding core control. Keep the lower back pinned to the floor; the moment it arches, the weight is too heavy.",
    "kettlebell_reverse_lunge": "The kettlebell reverse lunge steps back under load held at the chest or in the rack, sparing the knees while loading the quads and glutes. Keep the torso upright and let the front leg own the depth; the bell counterbalances the hinge.",
    "kettlebell_reverse_wrist_curl": "The kettlebell reverse wrist curl trains the wrist extensors, resting the forearms on the thighs and letting the backs of the hands hinge the bell up. Light weight and high control; the extensors respond to volume, not grinding singles.",
    "kettlebell_rotational_lunge": "The kettlebell rotational lunge sweeps the bell across the body into a lunge, blending a lateral step, a rotation and a squat. Let the hips lead the turn and keep the arms relatively long; it is a favorite athletic warm-up and conditioner.",
    "kettlebell_russian_twist": "The kettlebell Russian twist sits with the heels down and sweeps the bell side to side across the floor, rotating through the ribcage. Keep the chest tall rather than slumping; the harder the rotation, the less the arms should lead.",
    "kettlebell_shrug": "The kettlebell shrug lifts the shoulders straight toward the ears against heavy bells, training the upper traps. Keep the arms long and the elbows soft; a one-second hold at the top beats momentum.",
    "kettlebell_skull_crusher": "The kettlebell skull crusher lowers the bells beside the head from a locked-out press and extends back up, isolating the triceps. The bell's center of mass pulls the hands slightly apart, which many elbows prefer over a straight bar.",
    "kettlebell_squat": "The kettlebell squat holds the bell at the chest through a full squat, front-loading the body so the core and upper back work with the legs. Keep the elbows inside the knees at the bottom and the chest proud throughout.",
    "kettlebell_sumo_deadlift": "The kettlebell sumo deadlift pulls a heavy bell from between the feet in a wide stance, training the glutes, adductors and grip through a full hinge. Wedge the hips down to the bell, keep the shins vertical and stand tall by driving the floor away.",
    "kettlebell_svend_press": "The kettlebell Svend press squeezes a bell flat between the palms and presses it straight out at chest height. The isometric squeeze is the exercise: the pecs work to hold the bell while the press adds range. Keep the elbows soft.",
    "kettlebell_swing_clean": "The kettlebell swing clean catches a swing-height bell into the rack position without the extra vertical of a full clean. It teaches the punch-through that all clean work relies on; let the hips throw the bell and the hand merely steers it.",
    "kettlebell_turkish_get_ups": "The kettlebell Turkish get up travels from lying on the back to standing with a bell locked out overhead, through a sequence of deliberate positions. It is equal parts shoulder stability, hip strength and total-body control; move slowly enough that every step could be paused.",
    "kettlebell_wrist_curl": "The kettlebell wrist curl rests the forearms on the thighs and hinges the bell up with the fingers flexed, training the wrist flexors and grip. Use a light bell and a full range; the hands tolerate high reps here better than heavy grinds.",
    "one_arm_kettlebell_bicep_curl": "The one-arm kettlebell bicep curl curls a single bell with the free hand free, letting the trunk stay honest and adding an anti-rotation demand. Keep the elbow fixed at the side; the bell's offset handle keeps the wrist neutral.",
    "one_arm_kettlebell_bottoms_up_press": "The one-arm kettlebell bottoms-up press presses a bell held upside down by its handle, demanding relentless wrist and shoulder stability. Go far lighter than a normal press; the bell should wobble no more than a few degrees on the way up.",
    "one_arm_kettlebell_floor_glute_bridge_press": "The one-arm kettlebell floor glute bridge press bridges the hips up and presses a bell overhead from the floor at the same time. The bridge locks the pelvis while the shoulder works independently; it builds glute strength and overhead stability in one drill.",
    "one_arm_kettlebell_floor_press": "The one-arm kettlebell floor press presses a bell from the floor with the shoulder blade pinned, limiting the range safely and hammering the triceps and chest. The floor spots every rep, so heavy singles are fair game; keep the working elbow at about 45 degrees.",
    "one_arm_kettlebell_front_squat": "The one-arm kettlebell front squat squats with a single bell racked, demanding enormous anti-rotation strength from the trunk. The obliques on the unloaded side work as hard as the legs; keep the ribs from flaring toward the bell.",
    "one_arm_kettlebell_push_press": "The one-arm kettlebell push press dips the legs slightly and punches a racked bell overhead, borrowing leg drive to move heavier loads than the strict press. Time the dip and drive together; the arm finishes what the hips start.",
    "one_arm_kettlebell_row": "The one-arm kettlebell row rows a single bell to the hip from a hinged stance, loading the lat while the trunk resists rotation. Keep the shoulders square to the floor and pull the elbow past the ribs; the free hand can brace on the thigh.",
    "one_arm_kettlebell_shoulder_press": "The one-arm kettlebell shoulder press presses a racked bell strictly overhead, training each shoulder and the anti-side-bend core separately. Keep the forearm vertical under the bell and the ribcage stacked over the pelvis; equal sets per side.",
    "one_arm_kettlebell_swing": "The one-arm kettlebell swing swings a single bell between the legs and to chest height, adding anti-rotation work for the trunk and a grip challenge for the hand. Hike the bell back like a football snap and let the hip snap do the throwing; switch hands at the top or between sets.",
    "one_arm_kettlebell_tricep_kickback": "The one-arm kettlebell tricep kickback hinges forward and extends a bent elbow back to lockout, isolating the triceps. Keep the upper arm parallel to the floor and still; only the forearm moves, and the bell's balance demands a steady wrist.",
    "one_arm_single_leg_kettlebell_romanian_deadlift": "The one-arm single-leg kettlebell Romanian deadlift hinges on one leg while holding the bell in the opposite hand, stacking rotation onto balance. Keep the hips square to the floor, since the temptation to open up is the drill; move slowly and touch nothing.",
    "suitcase_carry": "The suitcase carry walks with a single heavy bell held at one side like a suitcase, forcing the obliques to keep the spine vertical. Stay tall and do not lean away from the load; it is one of the simplest and best anti-lateral-flexion drills.",
}
